{"sections":[{"xcodeRequirement":"Xcode 26.5","image":"ic_unified_ds.png","title":"Swift Package integration","projectFiles":"OUDS-Lime-Tutorial.zip","chapter":"Import of the Swift Package and choose its libraries","kind":"hero","estimatedTimeInMinutes":10,"backgroundImage":"ic_unified_ds.png","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS iOS is exposed through an open source Swift Package hosted on GitHub, and provides several libraries for your needs."},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"These libraries help to split products and make users able to select only what they need.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"SwiftUI is the only official supported framework for Apple platforms."}]}]},{"tasks":[{"stepsSection":[{"type":"step","caption":[],"code":null,"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Using Xcode, in your "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"project package dependencies"}]},{"type":"text","text":", add a new "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"dependency"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Search with the GitHub repository URL (https:\/\/github.com\/Orange-OpenSource\/ouds-ios), and select the "},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"ouds-ios","type":"text"}],"type":"emphasis"},{"type":"text","text":" dependency."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"You can then choose the "},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"dependency rule"}],"type":"strong"},{"type":"text","text":" you want."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"To know which version you need, you can have a look on the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Orange-OpenSource\/ouds-ios\/wiki\/01-%E2%80%90-Available-API"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and also the "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/github.com\/Orange-OpenSource\/ouds-ios\/releases"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Let’s say you will use some release candidate version today, e.g. the version 3.0.0-rc.1"}]}],"media":"tutorial-lime-1-ouds-swift-package.png","runtimePreview":null},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once you downloaded the package, you will see several libraries are available."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"They can be embedded inside your "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"target"}]},{"type":"text","text":" libraries."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Things are separated to let users integrate only what they need and embed the bare minimum of content."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSThemesContract"}]},{"text":" library provides the main elements like the ","type":"text"},{"code":"OUDSThemeableView","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". The theme contract is defined inside it."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDSThemesOrange","type":"text"}]},{"text":" provides the theme implementation for the Orange products, and contains also assets and all tokens for this theme.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDSThemesSosh","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" provides the theme implementation for the Sosh products, and contains also assets and all tokens for this theme."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDSThemesWireframe","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" provides the theme implementation for the Wireframe theme, which is a theme dedicated to mockups and prototypes."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDSThemesOrangeCompact","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" provides the theme implementation for the Orange products but with constraints of sizes and spaces."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSComponents"}]},{"type":"text","text":" contains the SwiftUI OUDS components defined with the Figma specifications, and also useful view modifers."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSTokensRaw"}]},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSTokensSemantic"}]},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDSTokensComponents"}]},{"type":"text","text":" are libraries defining and providing the tokens for low level (raw),"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"middle level (semantic) or component levels (high level)."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDSModules","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is for modules or rich components with extra logic."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDSFoundations","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is dedicated to some utilities and shared logic."}]}],"caption":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Add for example only the umbrella product merging all products mentioned above: ","type":"text"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDSSwiftUI","type":"text"}]}]}],"media":"tutorial-lime-1-ouds-libraries.png","code":null,"type":"step","runtimePreview":null}],"anchor":"Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries","title":"Import the Swift Package and the libraries","contentSection":[{"mediaPosition":"trailing","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDS for iOS is an open source Swift Package available on GitHub under MIT license.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"The package and the libraries must be added through Xcode.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"contentAndMedia"}]}],"kind":"tasks"},{"anchor":"Check-Your-Understanding","kind":"assessments","assessments":[{"choices":[{"isCorrect":true,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS is open source, under MIT license, and hosted on GitHub. Of course you can contribute!"}]}],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"I can contribute to OUDS using pull request","type":"text"}]}]},{"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The main supported targets are iOS \/ iPadOS. However we do our best to support macOS, visionOS, tvOS and watchOS.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"CarPlay specific cases are not scoped yet.","type":"text"}]}],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS supports officialy all Apple OS like visionOS, tvOS, watchOS, iPadOS, iOS and also CarPlay."}]}]},{"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"OUDS supports only SwiftUI.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OUDS provides UIKit components"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Which of these choices is correct?"}]}],"type":"multiple-choice","content":[]},{"choices":[{"justification":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You can import all products provided by the Swift Package, and tailor your choice to keep only the ones needed."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Even if we recommend to choose only the atomic products you need, the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSSwiftUI"},{"text":" product wraps all of them.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],"isCorrect":true,"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Some of the available products depending to my needs, or only "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OUDSSwiftUI"},{"type":"text","text":" if I am very lazy and don’t care about my app size."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"isCorrect":false,"justification":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"You need to chose the products the Swift package provides."}]}],"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"None, only the Swift package dependency matter."}]}]}],"title":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Which imports of the OUDS Swift Package products can I choose?","type":"text"}]}],"type":"multiple-choice","content":[]}]},{"title":"Introduction","kind":"callToAction","action":{"type":"reference","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Get started"}],"overridingTitle":"Get started","identifier":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-lime-2-intro","isActive":true},"featuredEyebrow":"Tutorial","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Welcome to the Lime theme tutorial! In this tutorial, you will learn how to create a custom OUDS theme by overriding tokens from the Orange theme."}]}],"metadata":{"category":"Orange Unified Design System","title":"Swift Package integration","role":"project","categoryPathComponent":"Table-Of-Contents-(lime)"},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-lime-1-package-and-libraries"},"hierarchy":{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(lime)","modules":[{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-lime-1-package-and-libraries","sections":[{"kind":"task","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-lime-1-package-and-libraries#Import-the-Swift-Package-and-the-libraries"},{"kind":"assessment","reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorial-lime-1-package-and-libraries#Check-Your-Understanding"}]}],"reference":"doc:\/\/OUDSThemesContract\/tutorials\/Table-Of-Contents-(lime)\/Import-of-the-Swift-Package-and-choose-its-libraries"},{"projects":[{"reference":"doc:\/\/O